Description: low-latency viewer for USB HDMI capture cards
 Lucarne shows the picture of a USB HDMI capture card (MS2109 and similar)
 with as little delay as possible, and sends its sound to the chosen audio
 output (Bluetooth headset, speakers, dock).
 .
 The picture is played by mpv tuned for live sources (no cache, no timing,
 one image of swap chain) and the sound goes straight from the card to the
 output through PipeWire (pw-loopback), so neither waits for the other.
 .
 A speed test measures every mode of the card (real frame rate, waiting time
 and decoding time) and picks the fastest one. The card's sound is found
 automatically (same USB device), cards and audio outputs are followed live
 when plugged or unplugged, and settings are kept between launches.
 .
 A key (S) saves the picture as a PNG and another (R) records the video
 with its sound: the raw MJPEG stream and the sound are saved while playing,
 then compressed to H.264 + AAC with ffmpeg in the background. A pattern
 shown on an HDMI output wired to the card measures the real end-to-end delay.
